│ patch_name               │ best-fit-after-placement-kvpr                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current greedy heuristic picks the GPU with the lowest KVPR *before* placing the      │
│                          │ model, ignoring the model's own contribution. Instead, evaluate each candidate GPU's KVPR │
│                          │ *after* hypothetically placing the model on it, i.e., (w_j + r/s) / (mem - size_j), and   │
│                          │ pick the GPU that minimizes the resulting KVPR. This directly targets the objective       │
│                          │ (minimizing max KVPR) and avoids dumping a large model onto a GPU where it dramatically   │
│                          │ raises pressure. A tie-break on remaining memory helps future placements fit.             │
