│ patch_name               │ binary_search_rebalance                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of a single greedy pass, this approach uses a feasibility-driven strategy: it     │
│                          │ binary-searches a target KVPR threshold λ, then uses a first-fit-decreasing packing       │
│                          │ (models sorted by density r/s descending) to check if all models can be assigned to GPUs  │
│                          │ such that each GPU stays under λ while fitting memory. This produces a much more balanced │
│                          │ placement than greedy, since the threshold forces spreading of pressure rather than       │
│                          │ piling onto the currently-least-loaded GPU. After finding the minimal feasible λ, one     │
│                          │ refinement pass moves models between GPUs if it lowers the max KVPR. This yields lower    │
│                          │ max KVPR at negligible runtime cost.                                                      │
