│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ binary_search_lambda_placement                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the greedy placement with a binary-search-on-KVPR-threshold approach, similar to  │
│                          │ the best-performing prior program (score 25.69). Key improvement: during feasibility      │
│                          │ packing, directly record model→GPU assignments, avoiding the fragile re-packing step, and │
│                          │ use best-fit (choose the feasible GPU whose resulting KVPR is smallest) rather than       │
│                          │ first-fit for better balance. We binary search the threshold λ such that all models fit   │
│                          │ memory-wise and every GPU's KVPR ≤ λ, then return the recorded assignment.                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
