│ patch_description        │ The current greedy assigns each model to the GPU with the lowest current KVPR, ignoring   │
│                          │ the effect of the model being added. A better greedy choice is to pick the GPU that       │
│                          │ minimizes the resulting KVPR after placing the model (weighted sum including the new      │
│                          │ model divided by remaining memory), which directly targets the objective. Also prefer     │
│                          │ GPUs with more remaining memory as a tie-breaker to avoid fragmenting memory.             │
