│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ local_search_rebalance                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of a single greedy pass, this approach builds an initial feasible placement with  │
│                          │ a best-fit decreasing heuristic, then iteratively improves it with a local search:        │
│                          │ repeatedly find the GPU with the highest KVPR and try to move one of its models to        │
│                          │ another GPU (or swap with a model on another GPU) if it reduces the maximum KVPR. This    │
│                          │ hill-climbing rebalancing directly minimizes the objective rather than relying on a       │
│                          │ single myopic greedy assignment, typically yielding much lower max KVPR at negligible     │
│                          │ runtime cost.                                                                             │
