│ patch_description        │ The prior failures came from division-by-zero when a GPU's used memory equals             │
│                          │ GPU_MEM_SIZE. The successful approaches used greedy assignment and threshold packing. My  │
│                          │ novel approach: (1) a safe greedy that assigns each model (sorted by pressure density     │
│                          │ descending) to the GPU minimizing the resulting KVPR, guarding against zero denominators; │
│                          │ (2) a max-min local search phase that repeatedly takes the highest-KVPR GPU and tries     │
│                          │ moving (or swapping) a model to a lower-pressure GPU whenever it strictly reduces the     │
│                          │ maximum KVPR across all GPUs — a hill-climbing refinement the prior programs lacked. This │
│                          │ keeps 100% success rate while lowering the max KVPR beyond pure greedy.                   │
