│                          │ λ, check feasibility by assigning each model to a GPU where it fits in memory and keeps   │
│                          │ the GPU's load/(remaining mem) ≤ λ; a model always has some feasible GPU as long as       │
│                          │ memory fits (since w/(MEM-s) ≤ λ for large enough λ, and the greedy fit by min resulting  │
│                          │ KVPR helps feasibility). Warm-start the search bounds: lo = max single-model pressure     │
│                          │ max(w/(MEM-s)), hi = the KVPR achieved by the greedy fallback packing. 60 iterations then │
│                          │ converge to near-optimal max KVPR, which dominates the greedy solution. If binary search  │
│                          │ fails to find a feasible packing at hi, fall back to the greedy result. This gives an     │
│                          │ optimal or near-optimal minimax placement while guaranteeing correctness.                 │
