│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ bestfit_binsearch_localsearch                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the current program (binary search + best-fit packing + local-search         │
│                          │ refinement) with the best-fit-threshold packing from the inspiration program. The key fix │
│                          │ is that the inspiration program crashes with float division by zero when a GPU's free     │
│                          │ memory hits zero (val = (W+w)/(rem-s) with rem==s). I adopt its best-fit selection inside │
│                          │ the feasibility packer (choosing the GPU with the smallest resulting KVPR rather than     │
│                          │ first-fit), but guard all divisions with a safe_ratio helper returning infinity for       │
│                          │ non-positive free memory. Then I run binary search on the threshold lambda (60            │
│                          │ iterations) and finish with the current program's local-search refinement that moves      │
│                          │ models off the hottest GPU whenever it strictly lowers the global max KVPR. This combines │
│                          │ the stronger packing heuristic of the inspiration with the refinement of the current best │
│                          │ program while eliminating the crash.                                                      │
