│ patch_name               │ add_swap_moves_local_search                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current local search only tries single-model moves off the hottest GPU. When memory   │
│                          │ is tight, moves often fail where a swap (exchange a model on the hottest GPU with a       │
│                          │ differently-sized model on another GPU) would succeed and strictly reduce the max KVPR. I │
│                          │ extend the refinement pass to also consider swaps between the hottest GPU and every other │
│                          │ GPU, accepting any strict decrease of the maximum KVPR. This targets the exact bottleneck │
│                          │ (the worst GPU's KVPR) and is a cheap, safe extension of the existing loop structure.     │
