│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lambda_bsearch_plus_local_search                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Restructure the solver as a three-stage pipeline: (1) a feasibility/lower-bound stage     │
│                          │ that computes an analytic lower bound on the optimal KVPR (max single-model pressure)     │
│                          │ plus an upper bound from a memory-aware greedy packing; (2) a warm-started binary search  │
│                          │ on the target KVPR λ, where each candidate λ is tested with several λ-constrained greedy  │
│                          │ orderings (each model goes to the GPU with best resulting pressure among GPUs that keep   │
│                          │ pressure ≤ λ); (3) a move+swap local search that polishes the best packing found. The     │
│                          │ binary search brackets the optimum tightly from warm-started bounds (instead of [0,       │
│                          │ 1e9]), and every feasible λ-packing is scored and kept if it improves the best-so-far, so │
│                          │ the local search starts from a near-optimal solution rather than a plain greedy one.      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0145                                                                                   │
