│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lexicographic_topk_balancer                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of the prior "move off the hottest GPU" hill climb, this approach minimizes the   │
│                          │ sorted KVPR vector lexicographically (min the max, then the 2nd max, then 3rd...). This   │
│                          │ escapes plateaus where the max can't improve but redistributing pressure to the 2nd/3rd   │
│                          │ hottest GPUs later unlocks improvements. It scans candidate moves AND swaps from the      │
│                          │ top-3 hottest GPUs (not just the hottest), uses randomized multistart orderings (inspired │
│                          │ by the Las Vegas recommendation but generalized), and keeps the best final max KVPR.      │
│                          │ Crash-proof: each attempt builds from scratch; failures just skip that restart.           │
