│ patch_description        │ The current algorithm is deterministic: models are sorted by density r/s descending, and  │
│                          │ greedy best-fit placement is highly order-sensitive, especially among models with         │
│                          │ near-equal densities. Since execution time is 0.00s, we can rerun the entire greedy +     │
│                          │ local-search pipeline ~30 times with small random perturbations (±2% jitter) on the sort  │
│                          │ key, keeping the placement with the lowest final max KVPR. This Las Vegas restart scheme  │
│                          │ can only improve the final result since we always keep the best candidate, and every      │
│                          │ candidate uses the same crash-proof placement path so feasibility is preserved. To keep   │
│                          │ the diff simple and avoid indentation-matching issues, I replace the whole function body  │
│                          │ with a refactored version where the pipeline is a nested function invoked per restart.    │
