│ patch_name               │ full_lexicographic_balance                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ A fundamentally different acceptance criterion for local search: instead of minimizing    │
│                          │ only the single maximum KVPR, we compare the entire sorted KVPR vector lexicographically  │
│                          │ (full lexicographic balancing). This pushes improvements not just on the worst GPU but on │
│                          │ the second-, third-worst, etc., which unlocks moves that a max-only objective rejects     │
│                          │ (e.g., a move that ties the max but lowers the second-highest GPU). We use multi-start    │
│                          │ greedy seeds (several orderings) followed by move+swap local search with the full-vector  │
│                          │ lexicographic acceptance test, plus a final max-only polishing pass. This strictly        │
│                          │ generalizes the K=3 top-K idea to K=all GPUs at no extra cost for small GPU counts.       │
