│ patch_name               │ any_pair_move_local_search                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current local search only tries to relocate models from the single hottest GPU. This  │
│                          │ can get stuck: sometimes the max KVPR can only be reduced by moving a model between two   │
│                          │ non-hottest GPUs (e.g., moving load from the 2nd-hottest GPU into the coolest one lowers  │
│                          │ the second-highest value after a subsequent move). I add an extra refinement pass that    │
│                          │ considers ALL (src, model, dst) pairs and accepts any move that strictly lowers the       │
│                          │ global maximum KVPR, running after the hottest-GPU passes converge. I also increase the   │
│                          │ multistart count and widen the jitter range for more diverse orderings. These changes are │
│                          │ safe (crash-free, only accept strict improvements) and keep runtime tiny.                 │
